{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And she spoke, etc., against Moses.</b> Perhaps they spoke to Moses' face, and reason concurs with this as well — for what would it avail them to speak ill between themselves? Rather, they said their words by way of reproof, and he heard their words. I subsequently saw in the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Sifrei) that they said thus, and they alluded to it in the verse ״וַיִּשְׁמַע ה׳ וְהָאִישׁ מֹשֶׁה״ etc. — meaning, he too heard."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:59.261019314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}